                <pb facs="0430" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7353b W 52/200: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-24T17:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                                1924—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>6. Chamber of Deputies has just approved finally Western Union contract. Report
                    by mail. Embassies London and Rome informed. Please inform Newcomb Carlton in
                    reply his letter 10th to me.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
